LIBPKGBUILD(3)

# NAME

libpkgbuild - native sealed package-build authority

# SYNOPSIS

*#include <libpkgbuild/libpkgbuild.h>*

# DESCRIPTION

*libpkgbuild* defines immutable build requests and results for native
Zeppe-Lin packages. Version 1 is an incompatible authority reset.

The library consumes one sealed *libpkgsource* snapshot, verified source
material, externally resolved and materialized build/check inputs, exact
architecture choices, and closed build policy. It seals those values into a
*build_request* before execution begins.

A successful *build_result* binds the request, execution evidence, complete
intended payload, and exact artifact bytes. A failed result binds the request,
execution evidence, and failure evidence and carries no payload or artifact.

# NON-GOALS

The core does not parse recipe syntax, inspect collections, resolve packages,
download sources, execute build programs, create isolation, write archives,
install payloads, query installed state, or implement historical compatibility.

# ADAPTERS

*libpkgbuild-plan* verifies exact artifact bytes through *libpkgimage*, proves
that the normalized archive equals the build-owned payload, and projects the
artifact facts accepted by *libpkgplan*.

# SEE ALSO

*pkgbuild_model*(3), *pkgbuild_request*(3), *pkgbuild_result*(3),
*pkgbuild_plan_adapter*(3), *libpkgsource*(3)
